WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.801
[Theme music playing]

2
00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:48.775
[Lord dondarrion] ...The wall blackhaven

3
00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:51.945
are unscalable vassalstone.

4
00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:59.244
And the castle is surrounded
by a deep. dry moat.

5
00:01:59.328 --> 00:02:03.665
It is well fortified against
any future dornish incursions.

6
00:02:05.042 --> 00:02:08.920
And though my seat
may be lesser in size.

7
00:02:09.004 --> 00:02:12.424
it is situated most pleasingly.

8
00:02:15.177 --> 00:02:17.804
[Clears throat]

9
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.976
[Pouring]

10
00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:41.495
[Lord dondarrion] The view
across the marches is inspiring.

11
00:02:41.578 --> 00:02:45.540
so said queen alysanne herself
when she honored my father and I...

12
00:02:45.624 --> 00:02:47.834
And tell me. lord dondarrion.

13
00:02:47.918 --> 00:02:50.504
did you think my great-grandmother
as beautiful as they say?

14
00:02:51.922 --> 00:02:56.718
This was half a century ago. Princess.

15
00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.720
Yes. it was.

16
00:02:58.804 --> 00:03:00.389
[All laughing]

17
00:03:00.972 --> 00:03:03.225
That was unseemly. Princess.

18
00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:06.103
The man is older than my father.

19
00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:08.522
It's unseemly for him
to put himself fonivard

20
00:03:08.605 --> 00:03:10.607
as a contender for my hand.

21
00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:13.318
Next!

22
00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:26.415
And now a child. [Sighs]

23
00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:30.043
[Man] The blackwoods are an ancient
house with a formidable army.

24
00:03:31.128 --> 00:03:34.548
In the riverlands.
they once ruled as kings.

25
00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:37.884
The blood of the first men
still flows in their veins.

26
00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.887
[Thunder rumbling]

27
00:03:40.971 --> 00:03:41.972
Go on.

28
00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.017
My Princess...

29
00:03:46.101 --> 00:03:47.978
Ours is a bond that has long endured.

30
00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.689
since Lucas blackwood.
the grandsire of my grandsire.

31
00:03:50.772 --> 00:03:52.607
aided the dragon
in his war of conquest...

32
00:03:52.691 --> 00:03:56.528
Aye. the blackwoods
truly turned the tide on that one.

33
00:03:56.611 --> 00:03:57.946
[All laughing]

34
00:03:59.197 --> 00:04:00.991
Coursed with the blood of the first men.

35
00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:04.161
our history is deeply rooted
in this land.

36
00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.455
which your house has made its home.

37
00:04:07.289 --> 00:04:08.957
If chosen as your match. Princess...

38
00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:11.251
Your days shall be easy

39
00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:14.171
and nights safe under my protection.

40
00:04:14.755 --> 00:04:18.258
"Protection"? The Princess has a dragon.
you dumb cunt.

41
00:04:18.341 --> 00:04:20.135
[All laughing]

42
00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:21.720
Bracken!

43
00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:23.430
I could learn to like that one.

44
00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.808
Let us have the next

45
00:04:26.892 --> 00:04:28.518
so we may go to supper.

46
00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:30.353
[Breath trembling]

47
00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:32.314
- Craven.
- [All exclaiming]

48
00:04:34.608 --> 00:04:35.734
We're leaving.

49
00:04:35.817 --> 00:04:36.943
[Indistinct shouting]

50
00:04:38.236 --> 00:04:40.071
Sheathe that steel. you twats!

51
00:04:40.864 --> 00:04:43.658
Send word to the harbor
and have captain oswin ready the ship.

52
00:04:43.742 --> 00:04:45.428
Princess. we're due in bitterbridge
in three days' time.

53
00:04:45.452 --> 00:04:47.412
I would happily row myself back
to king's landing

54
00:04:47.496 --> 00:04:49.539
if it brought an end
to this ridiculous pageant.

55
00:04:49.623 --> 00:04:50.999
[Man groans]

56
00:04:51.082 --> 00:04:52.459
[All exclaiming]

57
00:04:52.542 --> 00:04:54.085
- [Grunts]
- [All exclaiming]

58
00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:56.630
Don't look. Princess.

59
00:05:00.425 --> 00:05:02.260
[Music playing]

60
00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:21.071
[Criston] We should make landfall
inside the hour. Princess.

61
00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.826
How do you think he will take it?

62
00:05:25.909 --> 00:05:28.078
Do you speak of how you
rejected every suitor

63
00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:30.306
his grace put before you.
or how you abruptly ended the tour

64
00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.581
with two months remaining?

65
00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.211
- [Indistinct chatter]
- [Dragon whinnies]

66
00:05:40.715 --> 00:05:43.844
[Whining]

67
00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:47.848
[Warbling]

68
00:05:47.931 --> 00:05:49.850
Take cover!

69
00:05:49.933 --> 00:05:51.268
[Whinnies]

70
00:05:54.437 --> 00:05:55.438
Princess!

71
00:05:56.606 --> 00:05:59.192
You all right? Are you?

72
00:05:59.276 --> 00:06:01.278
- Fetch the maester!
- I'm fine.

73
00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:03.864
[Indistinct chatter]

74
00:06:04.781 --> 00:06:06.992
[Roars]

75
00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:08.827
[Music playing]

76
00:06:30.682 --> 00:06:32.058
[Indistinct chatter]

77
00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:54.789
[Woman whispers] It's daemon.

78
00:07:08.887 --> 00:07:12.140
[Footsteps approaching]

79
00:07:12.974 --> 00:07:13.975
[Fihuds]

80
00:07:26.237 --> 00:07:28.365
[Sinister music playing]

81
00:07:59.104 --> 00:08:00.544
[Prince daemon] Add it to the chair.

82
00:08:00.855 --> 00:08:01.856
[Fihuds]

83
00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.108
[All murmuring]

84
00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.081
You wear a crown.

85
00:08:19.749 --> 00:08:21.584
Do you also call yourself "king"?

86
00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:24.212
Once we smashed the triarchy.

87
00:08:24.295 --> 00:08:27.173
they named me "king of the narrow sea."

88
00:08:27.257 --> 00:08:29.968
[All exclaiming]

89
00:08:31.594 --> 00:08:35.265
But I know that there
is only one true king. your grace.

90
00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:42.272
[Music playing]

91
00:08:43.732 --> 00:08:47.819
My crown and the stepstones...
Are yours.

92
00:08:51.948 --> 00:08:53.867
Where is lord corlys?

93
00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:56.036
He sailed home to driftmark.

94
00:08:56.119 --> 00:08:59.330
- Who holds the stepstones?
- [Prince daemon] The tides...

95
00:08:59.414 --> 00:09:04.878
The crabs. and 2.000
dead triarchy corsairs.

96
00:09:04.961 --> 00:09:08.256
staked to the sand to warn
those who might follow.

97
00:09:45.502 --> 00:09:46.711
Rise.

98
00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:58.681
[All applauding]

99
00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:03.520
[Somber music playing]

100
00:10:10.193 --> 00:10:12.487
The realm owes you
a great debt. brother.

101
00:10:16.658 --> 00:10:17.659
Come.

102
00:10:22.539 --> 00:10:25.208
This is our chance...

103
00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:28.628
Daemon. he would venture off. abroad.

104
00:10:28.711 --> 00:10:31.506
- winning tournaments...
- [Indistinct shouting]

105
00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:34.050
No. no. no. no. no. no. no. no.

106
00:10:34.134 --> 00:10:36.219
I will not revisit this debate.

107
00:10:36.302 --> 00:10:38.471
You were always mother's favorite.

108
00:10:38.555 --> 00:10:40.723
No. it's no great mystery.

109
00:10:40.807 --> 00:10:42.016
You were.

110
00:10:43.434 --> 00:10:47.856
Our mother. she had no regard
for custom or tradition. rules.

111
00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:51.818
And I. sadly. was no great warrior.

112
00:10:51.901 --> 00:10:54.404
Congratulations on your victory.

113
00:10:59.909 --> 00:11:01.202
Thank you. Princess.

114
00:11:01.286 --> 00:11:02.370
[Birds chirping]

115
00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:09.294
Perhaps prince daemon
would care for a tour of the gallery?

116
00:11:09.377 --> 00:11:11.129
He hasn't yet seen the new tapestries

117
00:11:11.212 --> 00:11:13.214
- gifted to you by norvos and qohor.
- Oh.

118
00:11:14.257 --> 00:11:16.676
Would you like to see the tapestries?

119
00:11:16.759 --> 00:11:21.472
[Both laughing]

120
00:11:21.556 --> 00:11:24.100
[Viserys I] He has no interest
in such things.

121
00:11:25.435 --> 00:11:26.686
I'd like to see them.

122
00:11:27.979 --> 00:11:30.857
Then you should not deprive yourself.

123
00:11:32.734 --> 00:11:34.068
I shall enjoy them alone.

124
00:11:38.072 --> 00:11:39.741
[Viserys I] More wine.

125
00:11:43.369 --> 00:11:46.080
As I said. you were the favorite.

126
00:11:46.164 --> 00:11:48.917
No. you were. You were. I insist.

127
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.002
[Laughs]

128
00:11:56.591 --> 00:11:59.052
[All laughing]

129
00:12:04.849 --> 00:12:07.227
I surmise the tour did not go well.

130
00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:09.312
I endured it for as long as I could.

131
00:12:10.688 --> 00:12:13.149
To have every young knight and lord
in the seven kingdoms

132
00:12:13.233 --> 00:12:15.276
fawning over you...

133
00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.361
[Whispers] What misery.

134
00:12:20.323 --> 00:12:24.077
It is rare for girls in this realm
to get a choice between two suitors.

135
00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:26.162
no less two score of them.

136
00:12:26.996 --> 00:12:29.415
Those men and boys don't Fawn over me.

137
00:12:30.291 --> 00:12:31.292
They only want my name

138
00:12:31.376 --> 00:12:33.086
and my valyrian blood
for their offspring.

139
00:12:36.005 --> 00:12:37.966
I think it's rather romantic.

140
00:12:39.717 --> 00:12:42.887
How romantic it must be
to get imprisoned in a castle

141
00:12:42.971 --> 00:12:44.973
and made to squeeze out heirs.

142
00:12:45.598 --> 00:12:47.267
[Somber music playing]

143
00:12:50.311 --> 00:12:51.312
[Whispers] Sorry.

144
00:12:58.653 --> 00:12:59.737
[Inhales]

145
00:13:00.822 --> 00:13:02.156
How angry is he?

146
00:13:06.369 --> 00:13:09.330
The king went through
great effort to arrange your tour.

147
00:13:09.831 --> 00:13:11.833
He is... frustrated.

148
00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:14.627
But I am glad you are home.

149
00:13:19.299 --> 00:13:22.302
I find I have few friends lately.

150
00:13:23.594 --> 00:13:26.597
I like to believe
I'm still the lady alicent. but...

151
00:13:28.808 --> 00:13:32.729
All anyone sees when
they look at me now is "the queen."

152
00:13:34.897 --> 00:13:36.899
I've missed you. too.

153
00:13:45.575 --> 00:13:49.954
[In valyrian]

154
00:14:11.934 --> 00:14:12.935
[In English] So...

155
00:14:14.687 --> 00:14:15.730
What do you want?

156
00:14:16.981 --> 00:14:19.233
Only the comforts of home.

157
00:14:26.157 --> 00:14:29.577
I had not thought you
particularly comfortable in this home.

158
00:14:33.122 --> 00:14:36.751
Though I do suppose you seem changed
by your adventures.

159
00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:40.129
More mature. perhaps.

160
00:14:42.215 --> 00:14:45.009
You've matured yourself
these last four years. Princess.

161
00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.514
You'll get used to the attention.

162
00:14:49.597 --> 00:14:51.224
The attention I can endure.

163
00:14:51.307 --> 00:14:52.892
It's the rest I could do without.

164
00:14:52.975 --> 00:14:54.977
My father seems content to sell me off

165
00:14:55.061 --> 00:14:57.021
to whichever lord
has the biggest castle.

166
00:14:58.606 --> 00:15:01.025
There are worse things to be sold for.

167
00:15:05.988 --> 00:15:08.783
[In valyrian]

168
00:15:29.595 --> 00:15:30.595
[Prince daemon chuckles]

169
00:15:32.056 --> 00:15:33.266
[Prince daemon] Oh. [Chuckles]

170
00:15:39.147 --> 00:15:40.273
[Scoffs]

171
00:16:19.061 --> 00:16:20.605
[In English] Such a lonely prospect.

172
00:16:20.688 --> 00:16:22.857
[Bell tolling in distance]

173
00:16:23.441 --> 00:16:25.752
[Lord beesbury] The stepstones
were meant to be won for the realm.

174
00:16:25.776 --> 00:16:28.029
but over the past few days.
it seems we have traded

175
00:16:28.112 --> 00:16:30.448
a crabfeeder for a seasnake.

176
00:16:30.531 --> 00:16:32.825
[Lord strong] This is clearly a rebuke
for passing over

177
00:16:32.909 --> 00:16:35.119
lady laena for queen alicent.

178
00:16:35.203 --> 00:16:38.080
Years have passed since the business
with his daughter.

179
00:16:38.164 --> 00:16:40.208
Certainly. he cannot still be wroth?

180
00:16:40.291 --> 00:16:44.337
The sea snake is an over-proud man.
to be sure. your grace.

181
00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:45.963
That pride has been injured.

182
00:16:46.506 --> 00:16:49.300
Perhaps we can salve the wound?

183
00:16:49.383 --> 00:16:52.512
I fear lord corlys's pride
is the least of our worries.

184
00:16:52.595 --> 00:16:55.264
I don't wish to cause
you further distress. your grace.

185
00:16:55.348 --> 00:16:58.100
but my brother has sent
disturbing word from oldtown.

186
00:16:58.851 --> 00:17:01.979
Lord corlys is said to have
engaged in negotiations

187
00:17:02.063 --> 00:17:03.731
with the sealord of braavos.

188
00:17:03.814 --> 00:17:07.693
He plans to wed his daughter laena
to the sealord's son.

189
00:17:09.737 --> 00:17:12.907
If house velaryon
entered into an alliance

190
00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:14.825
with the free cities

191
00:17:15.993 --> 00:17:17.078
then_.

192
00:17:18.037 --> 00:17:21.541
We would have to seek
our own marriage pact.

193
00:17:25.211 --> 00:17:27.213
[Somber music playing]

194
00:17:37.723 --> 00:17:39.600
[Baby crying]

195
00:18:02.039 --> 00:18:04.041
[Crying continues in distance]

196
00:18:11.048 --> 00:18:14.051
- Good night. ser criston.
- Sleep well. Princess.

197
00:18:19.307 --> 00:18:21.017
[Exhales]

198
00:18:46.876 --> 00:18:48.544
[Sniffs] Ugh...

199
00:18:57.887 --> 00:19:00.306
[Suspenseful music playing]

200
00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:29.250
Whoa!

201
00:19:31.128 --> 00:19:33.130
[Music playing]

202
00:19:33.214 --> 00:19:34.382
[Wind blowing]

203
00:20:20.678 --> 00:20:21.679
[Rhaenyra gasps]

204
00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:23.431
[Chuckles]

205
00:20:23.514 --> 00:20:25.725
[Panting]

206
00:20:25.808 --> 00:20:28.310
[Music playing]

207
00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:35.776
[Rhaenyra] Where are we going?

208
00:20:42.199 --> 00:20:43.284
[People cheering]

209
00:20:45.035 --> 00:20:46.245
[Cackles]

210
00:20:47.747 --> 00:20:49.999
[Indistinct chatter]

211
00:20:53.002 --> 00:20:55.588
[Moaning]

212
00:21:01.177 --> 00:21:02.970
-Fuck off. boy. {933931

213
00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.265
he called me boy.

214
00:21:08.642 --> 00:21:09.894
[Men grunting]

215
00:21:09.977 --> 00:21:11.645
[Indistinct shouting]

216
00:21:17.359 --> 00:21:19.195
[People laughing]

217
00:21:24.909 --> 00:21:25.909
[Coughs]

218
00:21:26.243 --> 00:21:28.662
Do you wish to know your death. child?

219
00:21:28.746 --> 00:21:30.748
[Cackles]

220
00:21:33.876 --> 00:21:36.378
[Sighing]

221
00:21:46.639 --> 00:21:47.640
Let me take that.

222
00:22:02.655 --> 00:22:05.074
Leave us. all of you.

223
00:22:24.093 --> 00:22:26.512
You have a far kinder touch
than they do.

224
00:22:26.929 --> 00:22:27.930
Thank you. husband.

225
00:22:28.013 --> 00:22:31.267
[Indistinct chatter]

226
00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:36.730
[Man] And now we come to the matter
of the great iron chair...

227
00:22:36.814 --> 00:22:37.814
[Clanks]

228
00:22:37.857 --> 00:22:40.818
And whose bum it might bear.

229
00:22:40.901 --> 00:22:42.820
Our good king...

230
00:22:42.903 --> 00:22:45.281
Names his daughter.

231
00:22:45.364 --> 00:22:47.575
a girl. his heir.

232
00:22:47.658 --> 00:22:50.119
[Audience shouting and booing]

233
00:22:52.538 --> 00:22:55.541
But then to him. a babe is born.

234
00:22:55.624 --> 00:22:57.251
Oh! [Grunting]

235
00:23:01.297 --> 00:23:04.008
[Audience laughing]

236
00:23:04.091 --> 00:23:05.676
-A son! {933931

237
00:23:05.759 --> 00:23:07.720
[audience laughing]

238
00:23:07.803 --> 00:23:10.723
To which heir might the chair bear?

239
00:23:11.098 --> 00:23:12.349
Who will it be?

240
00:23:12.433 --> 00:23:14.727
The brother? The daughter?

241
00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:17.187
Or the little princeling of three?

242
00:23:17.271 --> 00:23:19.023
[Audience laughing]

243
00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:28.782
[Grunts]

244
00:23:28.866 --> 00:23:33.037
- Rhaenyra... the realm's delight...
- [Audience laughing]

245
00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:36.040
A girl so young and so slight...

246
00:23:37.207 --> 00:23:40.169
Loved by all of her people.

247
00:23:40.252 --> 00:23:44.048
but would she make a powerful queen.

248
00:23:44.131 --> 00:23:46.842
- or would she be feeble?
- [Audience] Feeble!

249
00:23:46.926 --> 00:23:50.512
[Man] Though aegon. the babe prince.
might long for a claim.

250
00:23:50.596 --> 00:23:53.766
he has two things rhaenyra cannot:

251
00:23:53.849 --> 00:23:55.893
A conqueror's name...

252
00:23:56.602 --> 00:23:58.020
And a cock.

253
00:23:58.103 --> 00:24:00.481
[Audience exclaiming]

254
00:24:01.231 --> 00:24:04.068
- Lies. slander! Boo!
- [Groans]

255
00:24:04.151 --> 00:24:05.778
Jest if you will.

256
00:24:05.861 --> 00:24:07.780
but many of the smallfolk
are like to believe

257
00:24:07.863 --> 00:24:10.741
that. as a male.
aegon should be the heir.

258
00:24:10.824 --> 00:24:11.824
Mmm.

259
00:24:12.576 --> 00:24:14.328
Their wants are of no consequence.

260
00:24:14.411 --> 00:24:16.664
- [Man whistling]
- [Chuckles]

261
00:24:17.331 --> 00:24:20.793
They're of great consequence
if you expect to rule them one day.

262
00:24:20.876 --> 00:24:22.336
[Audience cheering]

263
00:24:22.419 --> 00:24:26.048
For one night. I wish to be free
